--TEST--
A `secret` reaches an outbound request's header, form field and JSON document, which are the positions the sink rule deliberately leaves open — `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse` closes every *output* sink to a `secret`
// and names three positions it does not: a bound database parameter, a process
// argv, and an outbound request's headers and body. A credential has to reach
// the API it authenticates to, and refusing it here would make the qualifier
// unusable for its own purpose — the sinks that stay closed are asserted by the
// reject cases that carry that rule's name, `echo` and `Core\Json::encode`
// among them. Nothing below opens a socket
// (`rule:testing/an-outbound-call-is-answered-from-a-table`).
Core\Test::answerHttp("https://api.example.com/*", 200, {body: "ok"});

secret string $token = "s3cr3t-token";

// At a header, which is where a bearer token goes.
var $bearer = Core\Http\Client::get("https://api.example.com/me", {headers: ["authorization" => "Bearer " . $token]});

// At a form field, which is where a client secret goes.
var $exchange = Core\Http\Client::post("https://api.example.com/token", {form: ["grant_type" => "client_credentials", "client_secret" => $token]});

// And inside a JSON document, which the encoder walks to the leaf — the same
// walk `Core\Json::encode` refuses a `secret` anywhere inside.
var $session = Core\Http\Client::post("https://api.example.com/session", {json: ["token" => $token, "scope" => "read"]});

// What left the program is the credential itself, in each of the three
// framings: a record holds the octets a real call would have sent, so this
// asserts that the value arrived rather than that the call was allowed.
var $sent = Core\Test::sentHttp();
foreach ($sent as Core\Test\SentRequest $call) {
    echo $call->url(), " ", $call->header("authorization") ?? "-", " ", ($call->body() as string), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
https://api.example.com/me Bearer s3cr3t-token
https://api.example.com/token - grant_type=client_credentials&client_secret=s3cr3t-token
https://api.example.com/session - {"token":"s3cr3t-token","scope":"read"}
